"baseline_margin": -3.95, "analyst_adjustment": 0.95, "key_factors": ["R+10 partisan lean in an open seat favors the Republican baseline", "Recent Siena poll shows Gendebien up 4, but Democratic-sponsored polls show Constantino ahead", "All ten expert ratings call the race Likely R or better for Republicans", "Constantino has a fundraising edge and self-funding capacity"], "rationale": "The district's R+10 lean and unanimous Likely R ratings anchor the forecast toward the Republican, but the high-quality Siena poll showing Gendebien ahead 46-42 and the tight polling average justify shading the margin to about R+3 rather than the deeper Republican edge fundamentals imply. Prediction markets at 27% for the Democrat align with this read.", "watch": "Whether independent, nonpartisan polling confirms the Siena result or the race reverts to the district's partisan lean in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Elise Stefanik (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Elise Stefanik's retirement leaves this R+10 North Country seat open, and both parties have invested heavily. Republican Anthony Constantino has out-raised Democrat Blake Gendebien and holds a cash advantage, though outside spending has been minimal on both sides. Every major race rater, from Cook to Sabato, rates the contest Likely Republican or stronger, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-four chance.\n\nPolling tells a more mixed story. A Siena University poll in early October showed Gendebien leading 46-42, generating headlines about a tight race, while Democratic-sponsored surveys from Impact Research and Public Policy Polling showed Constantino narrowly ahead. The overall polling average sits near even, well inside the district's historical Republican margin, suggesting a competitive but Republican-favored contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1406, "margin": -6.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2036, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "202